I may have played this game a lot!  It's just so much fun.  And then, you move away from it.  Start playing something else... AND THEY RELEASE SOME NEW DLC!  The addiction starts all over.
If you haven't played any of the XCOM games I have to ask;
?  They are fun.  Every run through is different which makes the game completely replayable.  As someone who played the original UFO: Enemy Unknown (which then was rebranded XCOM) all I can say is that the XCOM series is a must own.

- Looks like a browser game;
- There is no animation for combat. Just numbers. You just create your troops and click on attack. No more than that;
- TOTALLY pay to win. You can increase your resources, your commander points, research speed, construction time, training time, arena ticks, everything existing in the game can be doubled with real money.

I'm a huge fan of the series but I absolutely can't recommend this poor pc porn cause of the side screen fillers;
Yes I understand that the game was launched around 2012, but back then games on wide screen still existed so there shouldn't be an excuse for sloppy port in 2015!
Arc System Works just wanted a quick fix money grab, rather to obtain huge profits from an un-tapped market that is the pc gaming;
They focus only on consoles and after 3 or more years we might get a release on pcs, a release that no one gives a **** about, none other than the fans of the series that even if they buy it they are betrayed by poor porting.
In the end what I would recommend, is think well before buying a great game with bad port, I for one couldn't accept this and I chose a refund for it.
